# Sample: weekly limit utilization report (UTC Sunday 06:15)
# Adjust paths for your host. Lupopedia repo root = first argument to PHP if needed.
#
# crontab -e (Linux/macOS):
# 15 6 * * 0 cd /path/to/lupopedia && php lupo-scripts/check_limit_utilization.php --write-report >> lupo-logs/cron/limit_utilization.cron.log 2>&1
#
# Windows Task Scheduler: Action = Program `php.exe`, Arguments =
#   lupo-scripts/check_limit_utilization.php --write-report
#   Start in: C:\ServBay\www\servbay\lupopedia
#
# Reports land under lupo-docs/reports/limit_utilization_YYYYMMDD.md when --write-report is set.
#
# NOTE: Scheduled cron/Task Scheduler entries are optional. Operators may prefer probabilistic or
# on-demand maintenance instead of fixed schedules; this file documents one deterministic pattern only.
